# The diagnostic for a sequential `for i in 0..<N:`, locked byte-for-byte as
# tests/diag/dotlt_sequential.err. The sibling tests/reject/dotlt_sequential.ty
# proves the refusal happens at all; this one proves it keeps SAYING the useful
# thing -- that the sequential replacement is the three-clause form, spelled
# with this loop's own variable name. Refused at src/tychoc.c:3507.
fn main():
    count := 0
    for idx in 0..<10:
        count += idx
    print(str(count))
